{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Nexus()"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage","text":"The sparse-set storage","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-archetype-storage","text":"The archetype storage","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" follows the design of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drops all tables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","text":"What the numbers say","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark"},{"type":"text","text":", see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Case"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sparse set"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Archetype"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.5 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"31 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.4 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"23 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6.1 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"227 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 200 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 800 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Random "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.get"},{"type":"text","text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"345 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 180 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4 900 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 730 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 510 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","alignments":["left","right","right"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyOneComponent"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents"},{"type":"text","text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick","text":"Which storage to pick","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often."}]},{"anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe","text":"Differences you can observe","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration order."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or your own key if you need one."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single-type spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Family spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the spans."}]}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Choosing a storage","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage"},"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/archetype":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"archetype","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Nexus.StorageKind.archetype","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One table per component set, a column per component type in every table, an index from entity to table and row."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/archetype"},"https://github.com/SanderMertens/flecs/blob/master/docs/ComponentTraits.md":{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","title":"component traits","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"component traits","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Entity/identifier":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The unique entity identifier.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EntityIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS16EntityIdentifierV"}],"title":"identifier","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/entity\/identifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift."}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs","title":"FirebladeECS","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Nexus","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(writing:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(writing:_:)","title":"componentSpan(writing:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Gives ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" write access to all components of a type as one contiguous ","type":"text"},{"code":"MutableSpan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"componentSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"writing","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV","text":"MutableSpan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2","title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/init(storage:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"storage","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Nexus","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"init(storage:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializes a new Nexus."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/init(storage:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The storage a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StorageKind","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StorageKind","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Nexus.StorageKind","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/SavingAndLoadingScenes":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Store a whole "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on disk and load it again with the same entities, components and entity identifiers."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/savingandloadingscenes","title":"Saving and Loading Scenes","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ComponentMacro":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement registration, cloning, snapshots and inspection for a component from its stored properties."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/componentmacro","title":"Generating components with the component macro","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/clear()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clears all data from the Nexus."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/clear()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clear","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"title":"clear()","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"abstract":[{"text":"A delegate for receiving Nexus events and errors.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventdelegate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}],"title":"NexusEventDelegate","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Rea